.TH GNOME-VOICE-SEND 1 "October 2026" "gnome-voice-server 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gnome-voice-send \- upload a GNOME Voice voicegram to a gnome-voice-server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gnome-voice-send
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uploads the recording made by
.BR gnome-voice (1)
\(em by default \fI~/Music/GNOME.ogg\fR and \fI~/Music/GNOME.voice\fR \(em
and prints the id and playback URL assigned by the server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server =\fIURL\fR
Server base URL (http or https). Default \fB$GVS_SERVER_URL\fR or
http://localhost:8085.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-token\-file =\fIFILE\fR
Read the upload token from \fIFILE\fR. Default \fB$GVS_TOKEN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-ogg =\fIFILE\fR
Ogg Vorbis recording to send.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-voice =\fIFILE\fR
Voicegram XML to send. Default: the \fI.voice\fR file next to the recording.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name =\fINAME\fR ", " \-l ", " \-\-location =\fIPLACE\fR ", " \-\-lat =\fIDEG\fR ", " \-\-lon =\fIDEG\fR
Metadata for the voicegram. When given, these override the \fI.voice\fR
file and it is not uploaded.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list
Print the server's voicegram list (Voicegram XML).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-delete =\fIID\fR
Delete a voicegram (token required).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only print the voicegram id.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gnome-voice-server (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Ole Kristian Aamot <ole.aamot@aamotinnovation.com>
